 C", -7.157594203948975]]}, {"t": "_COMPILER", "lp": -0.0001954627368832007, "top": [["_COMPILER", -0.0001954627368832007], ["/compiler", -10.159285545349121]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.00016929152479860932, "top": [["=", -0.00016929152479860932], [" ic", -11.585180282592773]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -0.0002351679722778499, "top": [["ic", -0.0002351679722778499], [" ic", -9.014782905578613]]}, {"t": "x", "lp": -0.0008549767662771046, "top": [["x", -0.0008549767662771046], [" x", -8.793863296508789]]}, {"t": " -", "lp": -0.0008490112377330661, "top": [[" -", -0.0008490112377330661], ["\n", -7.94676399230957]]}, {"t": "DC", "lp": -0.00019880125182680786, "top": [["DC", -0.00019880125182680786], ["D", -9.809717178344727]]}, {"t": "MAKE", "lp": -0.00016344929463230073, "top": [["MAKE", -0.00016344929463230073], ["Make", -9.549388885498047]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're using Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, which aren't on the default PATH.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag by flag:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` \u2014 **source directory** (where the source code lives)\n- `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` \u2014 **build directory** (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, efficient build system)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nCompile in **Release** mode (optimized, with optimizations enabled, no debug symbols).\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install binaries to `/usr`\n- Install libraries to `/usr/lib` (rather than the default `/usr/lib64` or `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE"}